course: dictionary
lesson: 6188
title: A hard word, said gently
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are sad, and people choose their words with care. «A miscarriage is when a baby stops growing and dies early in pregnancy; it happens quite often and is nobody's fault.» The sentence tells you the meaning: the baby dies early, before it could be born.
explain: People sometimes use softer phrases. «"Lost the baby" means had a miscarriage» and «"Pregnancy loss" is the official phrase for a miscarriage or a stillbirth.» Both are gentle ways to talk about something very sad. Look for the clue: lost and loss both mean something has gone.
explain: The word has another meaning in court. «A miscarriage of justice» means a court got it wrong and punished someone who did nothing wrong. This is not about babies at all, so read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
fact: A miscarriage is when a baby stops growing and dies early in pregnancy, before it could be born.
fact: A miscarriage happens quite often, and it is nobody's fault.
fact: «Pregnancy loss» is the official phrase for a miscarriage or a stillbirth.
fact: «Lost the baby» means had a miscarriage.
fact: «A miscarriage of justice» means a court wrongly punishes someone who did nothing wrong.
exercise: «A miscarriage is when a baby stops growing and dies early in pregnancy.» What does miscarriage mean? | A baby born very early who grows up healthy | A mistake in a letter sent to the wrong address | *A baby dying early in pregnancy, before it could be born | A long holiday before a new baby arrives
exercise: Priya reads «a miscarriage of justice» in a news story. What does it mean? | A baby is born too early | A football match that is cancelled | *A court gets it wrong and punishes an innocent person | A school test where everyone fails
exercise: Ben's mum says quietly, «We lost the baby.» What does lost the baby mean? | The baby was found safe | *Had a miscarriage, so the baby died before it could be born | The family moved house | The baby is lost in a shop
test: Which phrase is the official phrase for a miscarriage or a stillbirth? | Early walk | Happy birth | Baby party | *Pregnancy loss
test: Which sentence about miscarriage is true? | It only happens after a holiday | It is always someone's fault | *It happens quite often and is nobody's fault | It is a kind of football match
exam: What is the clue that «miscarriage of justice» is about a court and not a baby? | The word early | *The word justice | The word baby | The word stops
